; Publish the negotiate entry point UNDECORATED.
;
; XRAPI_CALL is __stdcall. On x86 a plain __declspec(dllexport) therefore publishes
; _xrNegotiateLoaderApiLayerInterface@12, the OpenXR loader looks up the undecorated
; xrNegotiateLoaderApiLayerInterface, does not find it, and xrCreateInstance fails with
; XR_ERROR_API_LAYER_NOT_PRESENT (-36) -- while the application runs perfectly and records nothing.
;
; On x64 there is no __stdcall decoration, so this file changes nothing there. That asymmetry is
; why the bug survived every x64 client and surfaced on the first 32-bit one (Far Cry 2, 2026-08-31).
;
; A .def rather than a linker pragma because the pragma has to name the decorated symbol, which
; only exists on x86 and would have to be #ifdef'd per architecture.
EXPORTS
    xrNegotiateLoaderApiLayerInterface
